  "id": "COMPOUND:21234 - PROTEIN:585",
  "verbalization": "Stilbostemin B 3'-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside appears to be a target of multiple compounds, all of which ultimately lead to Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. This suggests a potential mechanism where Stilbostemin B 3'-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside may influence the activity of Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase through a series of intermediate targets. The evidence indicates that the compound acts as a modulator of the pathway involving Cyanovirin-N, which in turn targets Colutequinone A and another compound that also targets Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. The shared target of these compounds on Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase implies a possible role for Stilbostemin B 3'-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside in regulating the activity of this enzyme, possibly through a mechanism that involves indirect interactions or allosteric modulation. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Stilbostemin B 3'-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside to influence the enzyme's function, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
